Given, $f(x)=5 x-3$ and $g(x)=x^2+3$
Let, $y=f(x), \therefore y=5 x-3$
\begin{aligned}
& y+3=5 x \Rightarrow x=\frac{y+3}{5} \\
& \therefore f^{-1}(y)=\frac{y+3}{5} \Rightarrow f^{-1}(x)=\frac{x+3}{5}
\end{aligned}

Now, $\quad g(x)=x^2+3$;
So, $g \circ f^{-1}(3)=g\left[f^{-1}(3)\right]$
=g\left(\frac{3+3}{5}\right)=g\left(\frac{6}{5}\right)=\frac{(6)^2}{(5)^2}+3=\frac{36}{25}+3=\frac{111}{25}

Let $I=\int \frac{f(x) g^{\prime}(x)-f^{\prime}(x) g(x)}{f(x) g(x)}\begin{aligned}
& {[\log g(x)-\log f(x)] d x} \\
